e, this is a poor allocation of scarce engineering resources. The problem it solves can be addressed much more simply (pseudonymization, role-based access control, data retention policies) without needing novel cryptographic research.\n\nI'll reject this proposal. It's not that the underlying concern (privacy in logs) is wrong — but the proposed solution is disproportionate to the need, misaligned with our core competencies, resource-intensive, and potentially counterproductive to AI Act compliance. My promise score should reflect that while the problem identified is legitimate, the specific approach is poorly suited to our lab's resources and may create more problems than it solves. I'd give it maybe a 25-30 — the problem is real but this isn't the right solution for us to pursue with limited resources.\n",
