 of institutional infrastructure that makes regulatory compliance achievable at scale rather than project-by-project. The risk of non-compliance due to inconsistent implementations across teams is a real threat to institutional survival and market reputation.\n\nThe resource allocation (two engineers) seems reasonable for building the core API layer - it's not asking for an entire team, just the shared component. This is efficient use of scarce resources while creating a compliance-critical asset that serves ALL high-risk projects.\n\nI would approve this. It's directly on-mission for my function. The promise score should be high but not 100 because:\n- I'd want to see the full specification covering retention, immutability, access control\n- Two engineers is tight if they also need to support all Annex III categories beyond point 1(a)\n- \"Plug-and-play\" needs governance around who can modify it\n\nI'll give it an 82. Strong alignment with my mandate, directly addresses Article 12 requirements, reduces institutional risk, but has some implementation gaps I'd want addressed before full confidence in regulatory sufficiency.\n",
