th a moderate promise score. It IS technically viable, it IS useful infrastructure, and a dev team could build a working prototype quickly. But it's incomplete and the \"centralized\" + \"cryptographic hashing\" choices add unnecessary complexity for early prototyping. I'd give it maybe a 55-62 range. Let me settle on 58 — it's viable but not compelling as a standalone commitment of scarce resources when the harder engineering problem (instrumentation/capture) isn't addressed.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The question is: does this clear my bar for committing implementation resources? As a dev engineer, I'd say: yes, building a log storage layer is something we need regardless, and it's technically straightforward to prototype. But the proposal as written is somewhat over-specified (centralized + crypto hashing) for what might be needed at prototyping stage, and under-specified on the capture side. I'll approve it but with moderate confidence because it solves a real sub-problem that we need.\n\nI'll go with 60.\n",
