hout being the primary driver. The risk is scope creep in the \"scientific study\" framing, but the core deliverable (automated probes integrated into monitoring) is bounded.\n\nI'd lean toward approve, with a moderate-to-good promise score. It's not a 90+ because of the open-ended \"research initiative\" language and the potential for the edge-case generator component to become a bottomless pit. But it's clearly above average — maybe 72-78 range. The alignment with existing infrastructure and direct regulatory need pull it up; the research framing and \"suite\" (implying multiple components) pull it down slightly from where it could be.\n\nI'll go with approve, promise 74.\n",
