        "content": "{\n  \"screenings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P2820\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This directly addresses my core concern of resource-allocation efficiency: Article 12's logging obligations (automatic event recording, timestamps, input tracking, database references) are non-optional and would otherwise be re-implemented ad hoc by every project team, multiplying engineering cost without adding scientific value. A single internal library amortizes that fixed compliance investment across all in-house high-risk systems, frees individual R&D teams from boilerplate plumbing so their scarce hours go to model development rather than audit scaffolding, and gives me a coherent infrastructure layer I can govern, update, and decommission as the regulation or our system portfolio evolves — which is exactly how existing R&D infrastructure should be leveraged under funding constraints.\",\n      \"decision\": \"approve\",\n      \"promise\": 83\n    }\n  ]\n}",
