ffs at each stage) is heavier than necessary and doesn't clearly leverage existing infrastructure. A more efficient approach would be to integrate a single logging-compliance checkpoint into an existing stage-gate rather than creating a new multi-stage protocol. The proposal as written would consume project-lead time and reviewer bandwidth that could be directed toward scientific work.\n\nPromise score: I'd say around 45-55. The concept has merit but the implementation is over-engineered from my efficiency standpoint. I'll go with 48.\n",
