t from the perspective of resource efficiency and actually meeting our compliance obligations within budget, it's over-scoped by an order of magnitude. The core compliance work (implementing logging in our high-risk systems) could be done at 10-20% of the cost this initiative would require, without the open-source maintenance tail or multi-institution coordination overhead.\n\nDecision: reject\nPromise: I'd give it maybe a 15-20. There's a small kernel of value (documenting patterns), but the proposal as framed is a resource black hole relative to what's actually needed. The \"thought leader\" ambition doesn't pay for itself in compliance terms. Let me say 18.\n",
