tion\" framing makes it a heavy infrastructure project rather than something you can prototype quickly and iterate on. It needs decomposition into per-system prototyping milestones to be truly useful from my vantage point.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. My job is to judge: does this clear MY bar for technical viability AND speed/quality of prototyping? \n\n- Technical viability: Yes, clearly. The engineering patterns are standard.\n- Speed/quality of prototyping: This is the weak link. As stated, it's a comprehensive institutional middleware project. That's not fast prototyping. But the IDEA — that you need automated logging middleware with an immutable store — is something you CAN prototype quickly on one system to validate the pattern.\n\nI think I'll approve because the core engineering insight is sound and viable, but give it a moderate promise score reflecting that as written, it's more of a program than a prototype-ready spec. 65 feels right.\n",
