nual overhead — very favorable cost-benefit profile.\n\nI'd give it a high promise score. It's not 100 because there are execution risks and the \"code comments\" angle is weak, but it's clearly in the \"would back without much hesitation\" range from my perspective. Maybe 82-85. Let me settle on 84 — strong alignment with my mandate, leverages existing infrastructure, bounded cost, clear ROI, but some execution uncertainty and gaps in full regulatory coverage.\n",
