cking\n- Con: LLM-generated regulatory documents carry accuracy risk\n- Con: Doesn't address core Article 12 automatic logging obligation\n- Con: Could create false sense of compliance if documentation looks complete but is AI-synthesized without proper verification\n\nI think I'll approve it at a moderate score. It addresses a genuine documentation maintenance need that supports our Recital 71 obligations, and the mapping to specific requirements is useful for audit preparedness. The LLM accuracy risk can be mitigated with human review workflows (which I'd insist on as part of implementation). It's not the primary Article 12 solution but it's a supporting compliance infrastructure piece.\n\nScore: I'd say around 55-60. It's useful but not critical, has risks that need management, and addresses a secondary rather than primary aspect of our obligations.\n",
