commits resources to a solution that doesn't actually meet the specific logging requirements of Article 12, particularly for Annex III systems.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The instruction says \"approve every proposal that clears your bar and reject every proposal that does not.\" My bar as compliance officer is: does this advance our regulatory compliance position in a way that protects institutional survival? \n\nThe drift detection concept IS useful for Article 72 post-market monitoring (which 12(2)(b) references). But it's NOT the logging mechanism required by 12(1). The proposal conflates these. If I approve this, am I committing resources to build a thing that partially helps but is mischaracterized as solving the problem?\n\nI'll reject. Promise score: 35.\n",
