rove the narrower scope (documentation tracking via version control integration) but the proposal as written is somewhat muddled in scope. Still, the technical direction is sound and feasible.\n\nI'll lean toward approving with a moderate promise score. The idea is technically sound for its core function, but the scope is broader than what's cleanly achievable in one tool without splitting into two subsystems. From a prototyping speed perspective, you could get a useful MVP running quickly if you focus on the Git→documentation mapping. I'd give it around 65-72.\n\nLet me settle: The technical approach is sound (version control + metadata mapping = feasible). Speed of prototyping: moderate — you can prototype the core in a few weeks but full coverage requires more work. Quality: good if scoped properly. I'll say approve with a promise of around 68.\n",
