prove this. It's well-scoped, actionable, and addresses a genuine regulatory requirement with appropriate operational mechanisms. The promise score should be high — maybe 82-85. It's not perfect (doesn't cover the full Article 12 logging requirements), but as a standalone documentation protocol initiative, it's strong and clearly within my mandate.\n\nLet me settle on 83 for the promise score. It's very promising from a compliance perspective, well-structured, directly addresses regulatory text, and has good operational mechanisms. The slight deduction is because it doesn't fully cover all of Article 12 (the automatic logging aspect) and could be more explicit about risk-management documentation.\n",
